@flexiarg math-formalization-CA/laurent-clearing-to-algebraic-polynomial
@title Clear Laurent Negative Powers to Reach an Algebraic Polynomial
@sigils [🌀/映]
@keywords Laurent, unit circle, trigonometric polynomial, Polynomial, roots, argument principle, winding
@audience lean-provers, complex-analysis
@tone heuristic
@difficulty hard
@subjects complex-analysis
@instantiates math-informal/reduce-to-known-result
@examples a95J03
@why no problem-corpus source matched (@holds-at absent; holds-token and id-text searches over every node in [problems futon-theory] found no match). Negative claim per the committed check futon2 holes labs library-loop runs l6_no_source_check.py, receipt runs/L8-no-source-check.edn. Rationale not invented (L8 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)
@how own mechanism: When the object is a finite Laurent sum over Icc (-N) N evaluated on the unit circle, multiply through by w ^ N to clear the negative powers and work with an ordinary Polynomial of degree at most 2N, where the whole root-multiplicity API (roots, rootMultiplicity, card_roots) applies. (source: this pattern's ! conclusion line; L8 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)

! conclusion:
  When the object is a finite Laurent sum over Icc (-N) N evaluated on the
  unit circle, multiply through by w ^ N to clear the negative powers and
  work with an ordinary Polynomial of degree at most 2N, where the whole
  root-multiplicity API (roots, rootMultiplicity, card_roots) applies.

  + IF: The goal speaks about a trigonometric/Laurent expression
    sum over Icc (-N) N of a n * w ^ n with w on Metric.sphere 0 1, and
    Mathlib has no direct integer-valued winding/index API for it.

  + HOWEVER: Polynomial lemmas (degree bounds, root counts, divisor sums)
    do not apply to Laurent monomials with negative exponents.

  + THEN: Define the cleared polynomial sum over Finset.range (2 * N + 1)
    with coefficients a (k - N); prove eval w = w ^ N * Laurent-sum via
    Finset.sum_bij (k ↦ k - N) between range (2N+1) and Icc (-N) N,
    using zpow_natCast / zpow_add₀ to relate natural and integer powers at
    w ≠ 0. Nonvanishing of the Laurent sum - z on the circle transfers
    exactly to nonvanishing of the cleared polynomial on the sphere, since
    w ^ N never vanishes there.
    + LEAN:
      api[Finset.sum_bij] api[zpow_add₀] api[zpow_natCast]
      api[Polynomial.card_roots'] api[Polynomial.natDegree_sum_le_of_forall_le]

  + BECAUSE: The factor w ^ N is a unit on the unit circle, so zeros,
    logarithmic derivatives, and winding contributions shift only by the
    explicit constant N, which the caller can subtract by hand.

@flexiarg math-formalization-CA/layer-cake-crossover-split
@title Layer-Cake Bound by a Crossover Split
@sigils [⚖️/比]
@keywords layer-cake, distribution-function, weak-type, Lorentz, rpow, lintegral, crossover, min-majorant, ENNReal
@audience lean-provers, analysts
@tone heuristic
@difficulty advanced
@subjects analysis, measure-theory
@instantiates math-informal-CA/estimate-by-bounding
@why no problem-corpus source matched (@holds-at absent; holds-token and id-text searches over every node in [problems futon-theory] found no match). Negative claim per the committed check futon2 holes labs library-loop runs l6_no_source_check.py, receipt runs/L8-no-source-check.edn. Rationale not invented (L8 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)
@how own mechanism: Turn a weak-type distribution bound into a local subcritical power-integral bound by integrating the minimum of the finite-volume and tail estimates on opposite sides of their crossover. (source: this pattern's ! conclusion line; L8 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)

! conclusion:
  Turn a weak-type distribution bound into a local subcritical power-integral bound by integrating the minimum of the finite-volume and tail estimates on opposite sides of their crossover.

  + IF:
      A layer-cake identity reduces the goal to an integral of a level measure D(t), and available estimates give D(t) ≤ min(V, C/t).

  + HOWEVER:
      Either arm alone is non-integrable at one endpoint, and direct ENNReal algebra obscures the scalar improper-integral calculation.

  + THEN:
      Split the positive axis at A = C/V. Use D(t) ≤ V below A and D(t) ≤ C/t above A, convert each nonnegative finite piece from lintegral/ofReal to a real integral, evaluate the two rpow integrals, combine their scalar values, and only then transport the finite ENNReal bound back to integrability and a Bochner integral inequality.
      + LEAN:
        api[MeasureTheory.lintegral_rpow_eq_lintegral_meas_lt_mul]
        api[MeasureTheory.lintegral_union]
        api[MeasureTheory.ofReal_integral_eq_lintegral_ofReal]
        api[integral_rpow]
        api[integral_Ioi_rpow_of_lt]
        api[MeasureTheory.lintegral_ofReal_ne_top_iff_integrable]

  + BECAUSE:
      The crossover is where the two majorants agree; assigning each arm only to the endpoint where it is integrable preserves the sharp subcritical constant and isolates ENNReal transport from real-variable algebra.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Separate zero-volume and zero-tail cases before defining C/V.]
    next[Extract C/t from the weak-type supremum and combine it with restriction monotonicity.]
    next[Prove the scalar crossover lemma independently of the original function and measure space.]

